fedora-dwm
==========
A personal dwm build for Fedora. Forked from suckless dwm 6.8, with a set of
patches ported over (and where needed, fixed up) from a previous personal
build, plus a Fedora-native install script.


Patches
-------
On top of stock dwm:

- pertag         - layout, mfact, nmaster and showbar are remembered per tag
- vanitygaps     - adjustable gaps, plus extra layouts (spiral, dwindle, deck,
                    bstack, bstackhoriz, grid, nrowgrid, horizgrid,
                    gaplessgrid, centeredmaster, centeredfloatingmaster)
- cfact          - per-client size ratio within a stack area (woven into
                    vanitygaps' layout math, not a separate file)
- movestack      - swap the focused client with the next/previous one in the
                    stack, instead of only cycling focus
- shiftview      - cycle the view to the next/previous tag
- statusallmons  - status bar text is drawn on every monitor, not just the
                    focused one
- status2d       - inline ^c/^b/^d/^r/^f color and drawing escape codes in
                    the status text, plus configurable bar padding
- setborderpx    - adjust border width live, from a keybind
- resizehere     - the pointer stays where you grabbed it when resizing with
                    the mouse, instead of warping to the window corner
- tiledmove      - dragging a tiled window onto another tiled window swaps
                    their positions instead of floating it
- unfloatvisible - re-tile every floating window on the current tag
- alwayscenter   - floating windows spawn centered (offset for the bar)
- actualfullscreen - MOD+Shift+f properly fullscreens a window, instead of
                    the bar-hiding monocle-layout trick stock dwm uses; also
                    supports a fullscreen-on-spawn rule in config.def.h

See dwm.1 for the full keybind list, or keybinds.txt for a plain-text
version (also viewable at any time inside dwm with MOD+space).


Requirements
------------
Fedora (or an RHEL-family distro with dnf). In order to build dwm you need
the Xlib header files - install.sh handles this and everything else below.


Installation
------------
    git clone https://github.com/zythros/fedora-dwm
    cd fedora-dwm
    ./install.sh

This installs build dependencies, the JetBrains Mono Nerd Font, dwm itself,
the patched dmenu fork (zythros/dmenu, needed for centered dmenu),
slstatus (zythros/slstatus), and the archlinux-logout power menu (MOD+x) -
then generates a session entry so display managers can start dwm directly,
or sets up ~/.xinitrc for startx.

install.sh deliberately does *not* install personal-preference applications
(terminal, file manager, screenshot tool, locker, browsers, etc.) - install
whichever of those you actually want yourself; every keybind that shells out
to one is guarded so a missing binary is a no-op, not a crash. See
config.def.h's keys[] array for exactly what's spawned where.

To build/install dwm by itself, without the rest of install.sh:

    make clean install

Edit config.mk first if you need to change install paths (defaults to the
/usr/local namespace).


Running dwm
-----------
Add the following line to your ~/.xinitrc to start dwm using startx
(install.sh does this for you):

    exec dwm

In order to connect dwm to a specific display, make sure the DISPLAY
environment variable is set correctly, e.g.:

    DISPLAY=foo.bar:1 exec dwm


Configuration
-------------
The configuration of dwm is done by editing config.def.h and
(re)compiling:

    make && sudo make install

Color theme lives in themes/theme.h.


Credits
-------
Upstream: https://git.suckless.org/dwm
Patches: https://dwm.suckless.org/patches/
Design reference (keybindings, patch selection, theme): a previous personal
dwm build, adapted and in places corrected for this Fedora build.
